# Keys pressed during fades (spec M1a section 9). The original remembers a press until the
# next hold asks for it. A key skips the intro; one during the Apogee fade-in ends the Apogee
# hold after one tick; one during the Apogee fade-out ends the Remedy hold after one tick.
# Every shot must match, with keys at the same stages of our sequence (ticks 15 and 45 lie in
# our Apogee fade-in and fade-out):
#   deadrally-headless find --key-at 0 --key-at 15 --key-at 45 --ticks 300 captures/keys/*.png
# Then neither logo holds: its 96 % picture shows in at most three consecutive shots (the
# one-tick hold, the 100 % flash, the first fade-out step), not for 2.5 s.
at 3000 key space
at 3125 shot keys-3125
at 3150 shot keys-3150
at 3175 shot keys-3175
at 3200 key space
